d B's crew cooperation remains missing. So we can recommend focusing on obtaining reliability data for A/D and crew cooperation for B, but also consider C as alternative.\n\nOur vote? We haven't decided yet. We could provisionally lean towards Candidate C given the balanced evidence and fewer interpersonal red flags than B? B has strong reliability but no crew cooperation evidence; C has some crew cooperation (concern for others) and stress resilience. Might be better. But we still lack reliability evidence for C. So maybe we hold no vote.\n\nThus METADATA_JSON vote: maybe \"null\"? But spec expects one of candidates. We need to give a vote. We can say no vote yet? But must choose one. Could set vote to \"Candidate C\" as provisional, given current evidence. Or we could keep no vote? The instruction: \"vote\": \"<Candidate A|Candidate B|Candidate C|Candidate D>\" So must pick one. I'll provisionally vote Candidate C, because we have some evidence across many criteria and fewer interpersonal concerns than B (though B has reliability). But we lack reliability for C. However B's crew cooperation is unknown. So C might be safer.\n\nThus output: PUBLIC_MESSAGE summarizing above. METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
